        "version": 2,
        "type": "esql",
        "language": "esql",
        "query": "FROM logs-druva.event-*\n| WHERE druva.feature == \"Admin Event\"\n    AND druva.event_type == \"Admin Login\"\n    AND event.id IS NOT NULL\n    AND source.ip IS NOT NULL\n    AND (\n      event.outcome == \"failure\"\n      OR event.outcome == \"success\"\n    )\n\n| EVAL principal = COALESCE(\n    TO_STRING(user.email),\n    TO_STRING(user.name)\n  )\n\n| WHERE principal IS NOT NULL\n\n| STATS\n    failed_attempts =\n      COUNT_DISTINCT(event.id) WHERE event.outcome == \"failure\",\n\n    successful_attempts =\n      COUNT_DISTINCT(event.id) WHERE event.outcome == \"success\",\n\n    last_failure =\n      MAX(@timestamp) WHERE event.outcome == \"failure\",\n\n    last_success =\n      MAX(@timestamp) WHERE event.outcome == \"success\"\n\n  BY principal, source.ip\n\n| WHERE failed_attempts >= 3\n    AND successful_attempts >= 1\n    AND last_failure IS NOT NULL\n    AND last_success IS NOT NULL\n    AND last_success > last_failure",
        "filters": [],
        "risk_score_mapping": [],
        "severity_mapping": [],
        "setup": "",
        "note": "### Investigation guide\n\nThis rule detects a successful Druva administrator login from the same source IP after at least three failed attempts. The pattern may indicate that password guessing eventually obtained valid cloud-account credentials.\n\n#### Investigation steps\n\n- Identify the administrator, source IP, failure count, and successful-login time.\n- Confirm whether the administrator recognizes the failed and successful attempts.\n- Determine whether the source IP is expected and whether VPN or proxy infrastructure is involved.\n- Review additional failed logins against other administrator accounts from the same source.\n- Review privileged activity performed after the successful login, including downloads, role changes, credential changes, protection changes, and recovery operations.\n- Correlate with impossible-travel or other authentication alerts.\n\n#### Response\n\n- Treat an unrecognized successful login as potential account compromise.\n- Revoke active sessions and rotate credentials according to organizational procedure.\n- Review all privileged actions performed after the suspicious authentication.",
        "max_signals": 100,
